From c31544e0a4ac7873a269d0139cc2dbceed8114e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 07:41:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10374/11362] Dashboard: report the WORKER, and make the
 generalization number carry its provenance

Two gaps I described in three consecutive hourly checks without fixing. Each was
costing four hand-run commands per check, and the first is the exact signal that
misled me for four hours yesterday.

WORKER WALK. The dashboard reported `job X: alive pid N` for the SUPERVISING
PARENT. On 2026-08-30 that parent showed 35 CPU-seconds asleep in poll while the
real work ran two levels down in a llama-server at 99% CPU decoding at 38 tok/s,
and I reported a healthy five-hour measurement as stalled four times running,
then recommended killing it. It now walks nvidia-smi's GPU holders back through
ppid to find the descendant of the pid given, and prints THAT process's CPU and
the last line of ITS OWN log -- discovered via /proc/<pid>/fd, because the
launcher's nohup log is silent for these runs and the worker writes elsewhere.
The walk is hop-bounded so a ppid cycle cannot hang the report.

It paid immediately: exp6753 now reads "worker 3306606 cpu 99.0% | task 1233123 |
n_decoded = 2326, tg = 32.17 t/s" instead of a bare pid.

GENERALIZATION PROVENANCE, and my own fix created this bug before the tests
caught it. Pointing the line at results/arc_leaderboard_eval.json was correct --
the adapter-free eval writes there, so reading only arc_loop_solve_*.json would
have left it "not measured" forever. But the first version then printed
"5 level(s) across 11 game(s) by live self-discovery" from a 48-DAY-OLD artifact
whose policy was `explorer`, the no-LLM tier-1 floor. A stale floor presented as
the current e3 measurement.

Age and policy now travel with the number: "[policy=explorer, 48d old]". The
reader can see at a glance that this is not the run currently in flight.

Also corrected two of my own earlier tests that asserted exact dict equality on
the returned mapping. The shape gained a `source` key and they broke -- an
exact-match assertion on a growing dict fails on every future field while telling
you nothing. They check the fields that matter now.

19 tests; 4/4 mutations RED (worker walk always None, policy/age dropped from the
line, leaderboard source ignored, zero live_levels counting as measured).
Restores byte-identical.

